menu "QRKude (styled QR codes)"

    config QRKUDE_MAX_VERSION
        int "Largest QR code version"
        range 1 40
        default 40
        help
            Size of qrk_code: version 40 (177x177 modules) needs 3922 bytes,
            version 10 (57x57) 412 bytes. The encoder scratch buffer has the
            same size. Lower it to save RAM when the payloads are short
            (version 10 holds up to 213 bytes at ECC M).

    config QRKUDE_NO_MALLOC
        bool "Never allocate memory in the core"
        default n
        help
            qrk_encode() then requires a scratch buffer (a NULL scratch
            buffer returns QRK_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT instead of calling
            malloc). The LVGL widget still uses the LVGL allocator.

    config QRKUDE_OPTIMIZE_SPEED
        bool "Compile QRKude with -O2"
        default y
        help
            The rasterizer evaluates the shape model per sample; -O2 makes it
            noticeably faster than -Os at a cost of a few KB of flash.

endmenu
